# Sandbox environment

You run inside an isolated VM. The workspace directory is writable; edits there
are immediately visible on the host.

## Network
{{if .Unrestricted}}
Public internet access is allowed on any port/protocol.
{{else if .AllowedHosts}}
Outbound internet access is restricted to HTTPS/WSS on TCP port 443, using these
exact hostnames:
{{range .AllowedHosts}}
- {{.}}
{{end}}
Subdomains are not implicitly allowed. Redirects and downloads from other hosts
require separate allowance.
{{else}}
Application internet access is blocked.
{{end}}
Host, private, link-local, metadata, and other protected destinations remain
blocked. This does not prohibit services running locally inside the VM.
An allowed target may still be unavailable or require authentication.
If access is blocked, report the required hostname to the user. Do not attempt
to bypass the network policy.

## Read-only host mounts
{{range .ReadOnlyMounts}}
- {{printf "%q" .}}
{{else}}
No additional read-only host mounts.
{{end}}
Reading these mounts is allowed. Do not edit, delete, rename, change permissions,
or write generated files beneath them. Copy inputs into guest-writable storage
if modifications are needed.
